                    insight_counter         : 'Located the failure at the counter: you asked tellers and agents to be faster and warmer, but the waits customers felt were produced in the IT and credit queues behind them (4.2 and 6 days against a one-day standard). With that diagnosis on record, satisfaction could not pass 74% however well the later rounds went.',
                    insight_diag_ads        : 'Named the advertising as the cause: the campaign was already promising 15 minutes against a 34-minute branch average, so a louder campaign could only widen that distance. The diagnosis capped satisfaction below the 75% target for the rest of the run.',
                    insight_diag_customers  : 'Named customer expectations as the cause: partly true, since digital entrants reset what a transaction should take, but it leads to no action the board can fund and left the internal turnaround times untreated. The diagnosis capped satisfaction at 74%.',
                    insight_symptom_ads     : 'Framed weak advertising as the cause: even with internal service named as the origin, the written diagnosis put the campaign behind the decline, and that capped satisfaction below the 75% target for the rest of the run.',
                    insight_symptom_both    : 'Treated satisfaction as both symptom and cause: a score cannot be fixed directly, only the failure that produces it. With that framing on record, satisfaction could not pass 74%.',
                    insight_sla_orders      : 'The two-day standard was resourced but issued as an order from the top: compliance without the internal-customer mechanism queued much less improvement, and cut branch time far less, than the same standard backed by recognition and shared scorecards.',
                    insight_adfix_underfunded: 'Advertised the fix: ₱350M went into the campaign while internal repair stood below ₱100M. The promise was keepable, but the campaign was the largest slice while the cause sat unfunded, and that capped satisfaction below the 75% target.',
                    insight_neobank         : 'Matched the neobank blitz peso for peso: the response moved the plan back to share of voice, cost satisfaction and brand equity, and marked the run as advertising-led, which capped satisfaction below the 75% target.',
                    insight_cfocut          : 'Took the CFO cut from internal marketing: ₱60M came out of the internal repair, the gap widened again and satisfaction fell in the quarter the cut landed, while the visible campaign was protected.',
                    insight_lag_denied      : 'Denied the lag: you told the board satisfaction would reach 75% next quarter. The internal fix sets that date, not the board meeting, so the promise bought calm now and staked the next meeting’s credibility on the tracker; in this run it cost brand equity.',
                    insight_ind_awareness   : 'Chose ad awareness as the monthly indicator: it shows that the campaign ran, not whether internal service is recovering, and it moves on a different variable from the one the board judges.',
                    insight_ind_satisfaction: 'Chose the satisfaction score as the monthly indicator: it is the outcome itself and arrives quarterly, after the decision window has closed; internal turnaround and engagement move first.',
